tion characterized by the buildup of lactic acid in the body, often seen in mitochondrial disorders like MELAS syndrome.", "STROKE-LIKE EPISODES:Stroke-like episodes are neurological events that can occur in patients with MELAS syndrome, leading to various symptoms and complications.", "MITOCHONDRIAL DNA:Mitochondrial DNA is the DNA located in mitochondria, which can harbor mutations leading to mitochondrial diseases, including MELAS syndrome.", "CLINICAL PHENOTYPE:Clinical phenotype refers to the observable characteristics and symptoms of a disease, which in the case of MELAS syndrome can vary widely among patients.", "TREATMENT OPTIONS:Treatment options for MELAS syndrome may include dietary management, exercise, and specific therapies aimed at managing symptoms and complications.", "DYSFUNCTION:Dysfunction refers to impaired or abnormal functioning, which can occur in various systems of the body in patients with mitochondrial diseases like MELAS syndrome.", "MITOCHONDRIAL DISORDERS:", "MARÍA JOSÉ MOLINA PUERTA:María José Molina Puerta is a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition at Hospital Universitario Reina Sofía in Córdoba.", "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO REINA SOFÍA:Hospital Universitario Reina Sofía is a medical institution located in Córdoba, Spain. It serves as a clinical management unit that specializes in endocrinology and nutrition. Additionally, the hospital is involved in the treatment of oncology patients, providing a range of healthcare services to meet the needs of its community.", "DEHISCENCIA DE SUTURA:La dehiscencia de sutura es una complicación postquirúrgica que puede ocurrir en pacientes que han sido sometidos a cirugía, como la gastrectomía. Esta condición se presenta cuando una herida quirúrgica se reabre después de la operación, lo que puede llevar a complicaciones adicionales en el proceso de recuperación del paciente.", "NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL TOTAL:NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL TOTAL, also known as total enteral nutrition, is a method of feeding that delivers all nutritional requirements directly through the gastrointestinal tract. This approach was specifically implemented for a patient following bariatric surgery due to complications that arose during the recovery process."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}